date: 2026-01-21

PROBLEM: end witness availability is not tracked by the type system, neither the end-witness requirement property
TODO/FUTURE WORK: extend the type system to track these too

what works:
  - location calculus EDSL model where the location are inferred by the idris type elaborator
  - sharing and indirection support
  - c backend
  - ADTs are modeled as Sum Of Products (SOP)
  - recursive functions
  - recursive data types

limitations:
  - functions have single arguments
  - byte sized tags ; either should have one bit sized tag
  - only I64 primitive type

FUTURE WORK:
  - end-witness tracking in the type system
  - sub byte addressing
  - pack multiple tags into a byte or machine word
  - multi parameter functions
  - more primitive types and primops, e.g. arbitrary sized words, byte-buffer
  - refactor to CPS style EDSL to prevent codegen duplications
